1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,680
In my tiny Pong, a perfect
defender loses on the sixth shot,

2
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,040
and nobody makes a mistake.

3
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:06,520
Here is why.

4
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:09,540
Pong is two paddles and one ball.

5
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:11,960
An essay I read says it
has no perfect defense,

6
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:13,720
and I wanted to know when that is true.

7
00:00:13,780 --> 00:00:15,720
So I built the smallest Pong I could.

8
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:19,100
I'm Tanmay Kulkarni,
in for Humanitarians AI.

9
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:25,160
Watch the rally. Shot one. Shot two. Shot
three. Shot four. Shot five. All defended.

10
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:27,220
Shot six. The ball goes past.

11
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,840
The defender can see
where the ball is going.

12
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:35,240
What it lacks is time, because
the ball gets 5% faster on every shot.

13
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:37,960
Two bars explain it.

14
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:41,080
The first is how far the paddle
can travel while the ball crosses.

15
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:45,000
The second is how far the worst
shot makes it go, about half the field.

16
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,960
If the first is longer,
a perfect defense exists.

17
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:51,940
But the crossing keeps shrinking,
so the first bar sinks.

18
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:55,880
On the sixth shot it drops below
the line, by about 8 pixels.

19
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:59,660
The arithmetic says shot six,
and a search that tries every aim agrees.

20
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:01,040
Nobody made a mistake.

21
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:02,540
The rally ran out of time.

22
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:06,920
It is only a model, with no
spin and no real machine.

23
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:11,700
But it shows that no perfect defense is
true here only because the ball speeds up.

24
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:15,260
The full film is called
The Rally Has a Clock:

25
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:17,720
When Is No Perfect Defense True in Pong?
